{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>All melakhah.</b> Rashi explained: even through others. And the Rabbi Moshe raised a difficulty: regarding Shabbat we say that amirah le-akum is a shevut derabbanan, but here it implies it is from the Torah. And one may answer: it is a mere asmakhta. Or alternatively, 'through others' that Rashi explained means through his minor son and daughter, and even though it is derived from לא תעשה כל מלאכה אתה ובנך ובתך — that is regarding Shabbat, whose prohibitions are stricter, but regarding Yom Tov it does not teach this." "<b>It alone shall be done for you.</b> A sign: בד\"ו פסח — meaning בד\"ו יעשה לך."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "The mnemonic בד\"ו likely refers to the letters bet, dalet, vav, i.e., the Hebrew letters with numerical values 2, 4, 6, as a sign associated with Pesach and the phrase יעשה לך."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:03.500024416Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}